    {
      "data": {
        "text": "<thinking> To create the Python file save_audio.py that writes synthesized speech audio to a local file using a concrete external provider, I will use the Amazon Polly service. Amazon Polly is a text-to-speech service that turns text into lifelike speech. I will import the boto3 library to interact with Amazon Polly and use the synthesize_speech method to generate the audio. The provider will be identifiable by the import of boto3 and the use of the polly client. </thinking>\n",
        "time": {
